# Under the input contract (PLAN.md) a signed comparison of operands
# of unknown range is read in the integers: n + %tid.x < n + 32 stores
# on the 32 threads below 32. An unsigned one also needs both operands
# nonnegative, which a parameter n is not known to be: a bound.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/setp_unknown_range.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unknown_range_signed
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on 32 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 32)
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store 128 B
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unknown_range_unsigned
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B (predicated)
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: global bytes: load 0 B, store <= 256 B
# Wrong output (PLAN.md): the third kernel sums in .u32 and compares
# .s32, read as %tid.x < 32 where n = 0x7fffffe0 runs the store on no
# thread; the fourth compares n with n & 0x7fffffff, read as false where
# a negative n makes it true.
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unknown_range_mixed
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on 32 threads in 1 warp (%tid.x < 32)
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_setp_unknown_range_mask
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B on 0 threads in 0 warps (no thread)
